From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 23:26:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] x87: keep zero signs and the status word's exception flags

FPREM's exact zero remainder takes the dividend's sign, and FSIN and
FPTAN return a zero operand unchanged, so FSINCOS keeps a negative
zero's sign too; the subtraction and the 128-bit routines gave +0.

Every F80 helper now accumulates the exceptions SoftFloat raised into
the sticky status-word flags (IE, ZE, OE, UE and PE), and sets ES and
B while an exception the control word unmasks is pending. FNSTSW,
FNSTENV, FSAVE and XSAVE store every exception flag and B, FLDENV,
FRSTOR and XRSTOR load them, and FNCLEX and FNINIT clear them. The
compare helper raises invalid only for a signaling NaN and FCOM, FCOMI,
FICOM and FTST add it for any NaN, while FUCOM and FUCOMI do not. A 16-bit FIST out of range
raises only invalid, through the conversion helper.

The arithmetic, compare, rounding and transcendental helpers raise
the denormal-operand exception (DE) for a denormal or pseudo-denormal
operand unless the operation is invalid, and loading a denormal
single or double raises it too. Loading a signaling NaN single or
double raises invalid operation; the inline conversion quieted it
silently. FYL2X of zero returns an infinity with division by zero for
a finite nonzero factor, and is invalid for a zero factor or a
negative operand, where cephes returned a finite value. FXTRACT of
zero raises division by zero, and FRNDINT and FBSTP raise precision
for an operand that is not an integer.
